{"type":"message","id":"dfbfc64e","parentId":"b623d6a2","timestamp":"2026-05-10T17:07:16.857Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01NXT8dFWwuMq4Uidt5Dh3Z9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"title:\tAdd SSE stream for Trail code reviews\nstate:\tMERGED\nauthor:\tdipree (Daniel Adams)\nlabels:\t\nassignees:\t\nreviewers:\tcursor (Commented), entire (Commented)\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1888\nurl:\thttps://github.com/entirehq/entire.io/pull/1888\nadditions:\t1690\ndeletions:\t4\nauto-merge:\tdisabled\n--\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\r\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire.io/trails/764\r\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nAdds `GET /api/v1/trails/:host/:owner/:repo/:number/code-review/stream` — a Server-Sent Events endpoint that tails a Trail's code review (live discussion thread) in near-real time. Emits an initial replay of existing comments, then per-poll diffs for additions, edits, and deletions.\r\n\r\nThis unblocks an `entire trail watch` CLI subcommand (follow-up branch) and a frontend live code-review view.\r\n\r\n### Naming note\r\n\r\n\"Code review\" here is the conversational thread on a Trail — the back-and-forth between author and reviewers stored in `repo_trails.discussion`. It is intentionally distinct from the existing `POST /review` / `GET /reviews` endpoints, which record formal **approve / request-changes** verdicts stored in `repo_trails.reviews`. The SSE event payloads still use `comment` / `comment_deleted` because each item flowing over the wire is a comment within the review.\r\n\r\n## Design highlights\r\n\r\n- **Bounded stream lifetime (~50s)** to stay within Cloudflare Workers request limits. Closes with `event: reconnect` so `EventSource` auto-reconnects with `Last-Event-ID`.\r\n- **Resume semantics**: `Last-Event-ID` header *or* `?replay=false` query pre-seeds the dedup map with current state and only emits changes from that point. The `ready` event also carries an `id:` line so resume works before any comment event has fired.\r\n- **~1s polling cadence**, with discussion-JSON parse skipped when `repo_trails.updated_at` is unchanged.\r\n- **Abort-aware sleep** so client disconnects close the stream in <50ms, not up to 1s.\r\n- **Per-isolate concurrency caps** (5 streams/user, 1 per (user, trail)) enforced via a small in-isolate registry; excess connections get HTTP 429. Explicitly documented as a stop-gap before DO-based fan-out.\r\n- **Structured per-stream observability**: OTEL span attributes (`trail.code_review_stream.*`) plus a single greppable log line on close with reason, duration, polls, events.\r\n- **Strongly-typed event payloads** (`TrailCodeReviewStream*Payload` interfaces) exported for CLI/frontend consumers; OpenAPI description documents all 6 event types with examples.\r\n\r\n## Event types\r\n\r\n`ready`, `comment`, `comment_deleted`, `reconnect`, `deleted`, `error`, plus SSE `: ping` keepalives every ~15s. See `docs/trail-code-review-stream.md` for the full spec.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n| Suite | Status |\r\n|-------|--------|\r\n| `api/src/routes/trails.test.ts` (11 SSE cases) | ✅ |\r\n| `api/src/lib/trail-code-review-stream-registry.test.ts` (5 cases) | ✅ |\r\n| `api/test/trail-code-review-stream.test.ts` (3 integration cases, real MySQL) | ✅ |\r\n| `pnpm run api:test:unit` (full unit suite) | ✅ 1525 passed |\r\n| `pnpm --filter entire-api run lint` | ✅ 0 warnings, 0 errors |\r\n| `pnpm run format:check` | ✅ |\r\n\r\nThe integration test asserts the full round-trip: connect with a real `ent_` API token → drain initial replay → write to `repo_trails.discussion` directly in MySQL → observe the new `comment` event over the same connection.\r\n\r\nThe full `pnpm run api:test` shows 33 pre-existing failures in `repo-sync-service.test.ts` and `sessions.test.ts` that exist on `main` (verified by `git stash` + re-run); this PR introduces no new failures.\r\n\r\n## Docs\r\n\r\n- **`docs/trail-code-review-stream.md`** is the client-facing spec: lifecycle, all 6 event payloads, resume semantics, performance characteristics, CLI implementation notes (incl. Node `EventSource` `Last-Event-ID` quirks).\r\n- The OpenAPI route description mirrors the doc, including SSE response examples.\r\n\r\n## Out of scope (explicit follow-ups)\r\n\r\n- **CLI client** with reconnect + `Last-Event-ID` propagation.\r\n- **Durable Object fan-out** so a hot trail with N viewers costs one DB poll, not N.\r\n- **Strict `Last-Event-ID` parsing** (currently used as a binary \"skip replay\" flag — sufficient for code-review comments, where dedup rebuilds from current state on connect).\r\n\r\n## Pre-merge checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Lint\r\n- [x] Format\r\n- [x] API unit tests\r\n- [x] Integration test against real MySQL\r\n- [x] Docs\r\n\r\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\r\n---\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> **Medium Risk**\r\n> Adds a new long-lived SSE endpoint that polls the DB every second and maintains per-connection state, which can impact load and resource usage if misused despite added per-isolate concurrency caps and time limits.\r\n> \r\n> **Overview**\r\n> Adds `GET /api/v1/trails/:host/:owner/:repo/:number/code-review/stream`, a Server-Sent Events endpoint that **streams Trail discussion comment activity** (initial `ready`, optional replay, then incremental `comment` / `comment_deleted` diffs) with keepalive pings and a forced ~50s reconnect cycle to fit Worker request limits.\r\n> \r\n> Implements a lightweight **in-isolate concurrency registry** (caps per user and per user+trail) that returns `429` when exceeded, and adds OTEL/logging instrumentation plus resume controls via `Last-Event-ID` and `?replay=false`. Updates `/status` endpoint mapping, expands unit tests and adds a real-MySQL integration test, and documents the SSE contract in `docs/trail-code-review-stream.md`.\r\n> \r\n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit eed7026f977c96c7de7ac017b040191246918131. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\r\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778432836857}}
